<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    file: deploy/launchd/com.jdfalk.whisper-tunnel.plist
    version: 1.0.0
    guid: 9c2f6b18-4d7a-4e35-a081-52b3e7d94c6a
    last-edited: 2026-08-31

    Reverse SSH tunnel publishing this Mac's loopback-only Whisper worker to
    the audiobook-organizer server, which then reaches it at 127.0.0.1:19848.

    Why a tunnel rather than binding the worker to the LAN: the worker stays
    bound to 127.0.0.1, so nothing on the network can reach it. Access is
    authenticated by the existing SSH key, and prod's sshd binds the forwarded
    port to loopback only (GatewayPorts defaults to no).

    ControlMaster is explicitly disabled. Without that, ssh attaches to a
    shared multiplexed connection from some interactive session, registers the
    forward there, and EXITS 0 — leaving a tunnel that works perfectly until
    that unrelated session ends. launchd would see a clean exit and, with
    KeepAlive, respawn into the same borrowed socket. The agent must own its
    connection or its lifetime is not its own.

    Replace USERNAME and PROD_HOST before installing; see
    docs/operations/metal-whisper-worker.md.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.jdfalk.whisper-tunnel</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/ssh</string>
        <string>-N</string>
        <!-- Own the connection; never ride a shared master. -->
        <string>-o</string><string>ControlMaster=no</string>
        <string>-o</string><string>ControlPath=none</string>
        <!-- Fail loudly if the remote port is taken, so KeepAlive retries
             instead of leaving a live ssh with no forward behind it. -->
        <string>-o</string><string>ExitOnForwardFailure=yes</string>
        <string>-o</string><string>ServerAliveInterval=30</string>
        <string>-o</string><string>ServerAliveCountMax=3</string>
        <string>-o</string><string>BatchMode=yes</string>
        <string>-o</string><string>StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new</string>
        <string>-R</string><string>19848:127.0.0.1:19848</string>
        <string>USERNAME@PROD_HOST</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>30</integer>
    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/whisper-tunnel.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/whisper-tunnel.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
